# An access inside the length names a guard that proves the position of that access below the length of that array, and its store a guard that proves storage of the array's own. The guards last until the kind, the place or the length of the array may change: a store inside the length changes none of them, whichever array it hits
# FORM: Prepared
# RUN: verify
# DIAGNOSTIC: InvalidGuard 4
# DIAGNOSTIC: GuardNotAvailable 4
# DIAGNOSTIC: OperandTypeMismatch 2
# DIAGNOSTIC: PayloadOutOfRange 1

